Table full name: bigquery-public-data.nhtsa_traffic_fatalities. parkwork_2015
Column name: consecutive_number Type: INT64 Description: This data element is the unique case number assigned to each crash. It appears on each data file and is used to merge information from the data files together. xxxxxx Two Characters for State Code followed by Four Characters for Case Number
Column name: hour_of_crash Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the hour at which the crash occurred.0-23 Hour 99 Unknown
Column name: first_harmful_event Type: INT64 Description: This data element describes the first injury or damage producing event of the crash.For more info on the codes, please look at <C19 First Harmful Event> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: manner_of_collision Type: INT64 Description: This data element describes the orientation of two motor vehicles in-transport when they are involved in the “First Harmful Event” of a collision crash. If the “First Harmful Event” is not a collision between two motor vehicles in-transport it is classified as such.For more info on the codes, please look at <C20 Manner of Collision> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: body_type Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies a classification of this vehicle based on its general body configuration, size, shape, doors, etc.For more info on the codes, please look at <V11 Body Type> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: extent_of_damage Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the amount of damage sustained by this vehicle as indicated on the PAR based on an operational damage scale.0 No Damage 2 Minor Damage 4 Functional Damage 6 Disabling Damage 8 Not Reported 9 Unknown
Column name: vehicle_removal Type: INT64 Description: This data element describes the mode by which this vehicle left the scene of the crash.-- Driven Away -- Towed Away 2 Towed Due to Disabling Damage -- Abandoned/Left Scene 3 Towed Not Due to Disabling Damage -- Abandoned/Left Scene 5 Not Towed 8 Not Reported 9 Unknown
Column name: most_harmful_event Type: INT64 Description: This data element describes the event that resulted in the most severe injury or, if no injury, the greatest property damage involving this vehicle.For more info on the codes, please look at <V32 Most Harmful Event> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: related_factors_vehicle_level1 Type: INT64 Description: This data element records factors related to this vehicle expressed by the investigating officer.For more info on the codes, please look at <V33 Related Factors – Vehicle Level> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Sample rows:
[{'consecutive_number': 61702, 'hour_of_crash': 13, 'first_harmful_event': 73, 'manner_of_collision': 0, 'body_type': 20, 'extent_of_damage': 0, 'vehicle_removal': 5, 'most_harmful_event': 73, 'related_factors_vehicle_level1': 0}, {'consecutive_number': 62719, 'hour_of_crash': 10, 'first_harmful_event': 7, 'manner_of_collision': 0, 'body_type': 14, 'extent_of_damage': 2, 'vehicle_removal': 5, 'most_harmful_event': 12, 'related_factors_vehicle_level1': 0}, {'consecutive_number': 120249, 'hour_of_crash': 1, 'first_harmful_event': 32, 'manner_of_collision': 0, 'body_type': 30, 'extent_of_damage': 4, 'vehicle_removal': 5, 'most_harmful_event': 12, 'related_factors_vehicle_level1': 0}, {'consecutive_number': 120249, 'hour_of_crash': 1, 'first_harmful_event': 32, 'manner_of_collision': 0, 'body_type': 14, 'extent_of_damage': 2, 'vehicle_removal': 5, 'most_harmful_event': 12, 'related_factors_vehicle_level1': 0}, {'consecutive_number': 130118, 'hour_of_crash': 3, 'first_harmful_event': 24, 'manner_of_collision': 0, 'body_type': 4, 'extent_of_damage': 6, 'vehicle_removal': 2, 'most_harmful_event': 12, 'related_factors_vehicle_level1': 0}]

